messages.reasoning:
Wait — `enrolled()` creates a NEW student each call. In the average test, the second `enrolled()` creates a different student! That's wrong: both courses must be enrolled by the SAME student.

Fix: add a helper `enrollExisting(Student $student, array $attrs)` or make enrolled() accept a student.

Let me restructure: 

```php
private function enroll(Student $student, array $courseAttributes = []): Course
{
    $course = Course::factory()->create($courseAttributes);
    CourseEnrollment::enroll($student, $course)->confirm();
    return $course;
}

private function enrolled(array $attrs = []): array
{
    $student = Student::factory()->create();
    return [$student, $this->enroll($student, $attrs)];
}
```

Then in average test: `[$student] = $this->enrolled(['title'=>'دورهٔ نمره‌دار']); $this->enroll($student, ['title'=>'دورهٔ بی‌نمره']);`

Also the cancelled test uses its own code — fine.

Let me patch.

